  "coverage_notes": [
    "The authoritative design demonstrates streaming verification through persisted run state and ordered event logs, not through a push transport such as websockets or server-sent events.",
    "The frontend must use polling for live updates because no push-stream endpoint exists in the API contract.",
    "The timeout watch threshold is fixed by the authoritative query pattern at the default behavior; UI customization beyond that is out of scope for this POV.",
    "No standalone execution-orchestration endpoint exists; creating or updating runs represents POV simulation/tracking of workflow execution state."
  ]
